## Current Physical Authority Applied

- Pink Pepper EO/Base is absent from the live inventory. No procurement follows from this target.
- Black Pepper EO, Rose Oxide 1%, Damascone Beta 10% in DPG, and Geraniol 10% in DPG remain an explicitly **non-equivalent** reconstruction hypothesis.
- Habanolide, Romandolide, and Ethylene Brassylate are owned neat. Only Habanolide appears in the V1.3 dosing table; the others are alternative one-musk arms, never additions to it.
- Parmavert and every tincture are unavailable; none is used.
- Lemonile is restricted to its existing 1% DPG stock and is not used.
- Clearwood is owned neat. Ambrox Super is the nominal 33% w/v DEP:ethanol stock; exact w/w and volume-active equivalence remain **HOLD**.
- BONTAUX authority applies only to `Lavender EO (BONTAUX SAS)`.
- No cinnamon or lactone is used. The AP-T1-only Cinnamon Bark exception has no authority here.
- Every direct formula aliquot is at least 10 uL. The Peppermint 10% working stock remains future, unprepared, and unauthorized.

## Named Identity and Hedonic Contract

**Name:** Silver Traverse.  
**Subject:** charged technical sailcloth carrying luminous Pink Pepper.  
**Main note:** Pink Pepper — rosy, effervescent, berry-bright, tensile, and gently woody-spicy; never hot culinary Black Pepper or literal rose.  
**Cold state:** pepper sparks cross bitter peel, wet silver-mineral air, and taut lavender-linalyl cloth.  
**Warm state:** the same cloth dries and flexes while mineral amber, transparent wood, vetiver, patchouli, Cashmeran, and skin warmth reveal its interior.  
**Invariant cue:** rosy-pepper pressure remains classifiable through the aromatic heart and returns as dry woody-spice grain.  
**Emotional effect:** alert forward motion followed by bodily ease; sporty without shower-gel cheerfulness and luxurious without powder, leather, or sweetness.

### Hedonic rebase hypothesis

| Path | V1.3 owners | Intended effect | Failure to record |
|---|---|---|---|
| Tension | protected Pink Pepper nucleus; Black Pepper pressure; narrow aldehydic/mineral points; restrained dry woods | attention and forward pull | hot/dry pepper, metallic harshness, rigid amberwood, fatigue |
| Comfort | Habanolide skin veil, Cashmeran flex, Hexyl Salicylate cloth, trace Coumarin warmth | tactile bodily ease without gourmand sweetness | laundry musk, powder, cream, blank musky softness |
| Release | Hedione, Helional, Dihydrojasmone, Hexyl Salicylate, and declared Benzyl Benzoate negative space | opening pressure opens into a breathable middle and yielding interior | diffuse generic freshness, hollowing, compensator detection |
| Re-smell moment | 30-120 minute transfer from rosy pepper/lavender cloth into warm dry textile grain | curiosity through transformation rather than brute strength | first-object loss, hard seam, generic ambrox drydown |

The broad reference interval remains Prada Luna Rossa's athletic lavender/mint/amber surface and Montblanc Explorer/Explorer Extreme's Pink-Pepper/bergamot/aromatic-to-patchouli/amber trajectory. Creed Aventus contributes no protected ingredient identity; any resemblance through the Explorer family is limited to an abstract fresh-to-dry woody-amber motion. Pineapple, birch/leather, fruity smoke, and an Aventus reconstruction are excluded.

### Takeover exclusions

- reject lavender, Dihydromyrcenol, citrus, Hedione, Iso E Super, ambrox, or musk becoming a more accurate name than Pink Pepper;
- reject literal rose, lychee, plum, lipstick, iris, cosmetic powder, or violet makeup;
- reject hot, dry, culinary Black Pepper or trigeminal aggression;
- reject calone/melon, generic blue shower gel, mint candy, or marine identity;
- reject Aventus-like pineapple, birch smoke, leather, fruit-chypre, or oakmoss identity;
- reject oud, rum, creamy sandalwood, vanilla/tonka sweetness, or laundry musk;
- reject a soft but anonymous base that loses the peppered technical textile.

## Structural Architecture

| Dimension | V1.3 construction | Future physical success criterion |
|---|---|---|
| One subject / cold state | exact Pink Pepper hero in TARGET; CURRENT spicy pressure plus metallic-rosy surface and berry-woody echo on taut aromatic cloth | one luminous rosy-effervescent pepper object, not Black Pepper plus rose |
| One subject / warm state | the same cloth warmed by mineral amber, transparent patchouli wood, Cashmeran, vetiver, and one inward musk veil | dry, flexed, skin-warm textile that still names the opening subject |
| Front glint | Pink Pepper; halved Bergamot/Cedrat; Methyl Pamplemousse; Aldehyde C10; Peppermint trace; Scentenal | pepper first; citrus is edge and dimension rather than a second object |
| Near body | reduced BONTAUX lavender, Linalyl Acetate, Ethyl Linalool, Clary Sage, Geraniol | recognizable athletic cloth below the hero without masking it |
| Living middle | moderated Hedione, increased Helional, Dihydrojasmone, and Hexyl Salicylate; reduced Cyclamen | breathable, moving cloth and pressure release without Hedione or muguet glare |
| Rear contour | reduced Iso E, Ambrox, Timberol, and Ambermax; V1.2 Clearwood/Azarbre body retained with vetiver, patchouli, Cashmeran, and trace resin | preserve rounded rear depth while trimming abstract and rigid pressure |
| Skin/fabric echo | Habanolide, Cashmeran, patchouli, vetiver, Iso E, Hexyl Salicylate | intimate textile memory rather than laundry bloom or detached musk |
| Pressure / release | Pink-Pepper nucleus and narrow cool points / expanded middle, salicylate cloth, quiet mass, skin veil | repeated desire to re-smell without harshness, fatigue, or collapse |
| Temporal recurrence | pepper-peel sparkle -> rosy lavender cloth -> dry pepper-earth/vetiver/Cashmeran grain | late phase recalls the subject rather than merely retaining woods |
| Opposed texture | sparkling, wet-cool, taut surface / dry, yielding, warm interior | both textures remain one sailcloth object |
| Identity-bearing base | peppered aromatic fabric persists through the softened woody-amber rear | base cannot be detached and called generic sporty ambrox |

Every criterion is **NOT TESTED**.

