## Material Alternatives and Rejections

| Register | Selected | Alternatives reviewed | Decision |
|---|---|---|---|
| exact hero | Pink Pepper EO in TARGET | proprietary Pink Pepper Base | exact EO keeps the identity target explicit; both remain supplier-specific and unavailable |
| CURRENT pressure | Black Pepper EO | Cardamom, Ginger, Ethyl Safranate | only Black Pepper supplies owned pepper pressure; alternatives introduce cineole, a second spice subject, or leather-metal drift |
| citrus | half-dose Bergamot + Cedrat + trace Methyl Pamplemousse | Lemon FCF, Red Mandarin, Grapefruit FCF, more citrus | the selected set retains peel shape with less glare; extra citrus would create a competing object |
| middle release | Hedione + Helional + Dihydrojasmone + Hexyl Salicylate | Hedione HC, Florol, Mayol, Benzyl Salicylate | selected materials divide bloom, wet depth, motion, and cloth; alternatives duplicate radiance or add muguet/cosmetic wax |
| rear structure | softened Ambrox/Iso E/Clearwood/Azarbre/Timberol/Ambermax | more amberwood, cedar, sandalwood, Norlimbanol | existing rear already has all required planes; another wood would add pressure or a new identity rather than hedonism |
| sole musk | Habanolide | Romandolide, Ethylene Brassylate, Ambrettolide 10%, no musk | Habanolide tests inward skin release because Iso E/Hedione already carry outward diffusion; Romandolide may preserve technical projection better, EB may become creamy/lactonic, Ambrettolide may become fruity-naturalistic, and no musk may be clearest. None is selected by theory alone. |

## TARGET / CURRENT Gap and Missing-Chemical Impact Gate

| TARGET item | CURRENT translation | Residual limitation / severity | Claim ceiling | Procurement |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Pink Pepper EO hero | Black Pepper + Rose Oxide + Damascone Beta + Geraniol | **critical identity gap:** may read hot, dry, rose-like, plummy, or fragmented | identity/equivalence HOLD; sensory NOT TESTED | NOT AUTHORIZED |
| Rectified spearmint | future 10% stock of owned Peppermint EO | moderate state gap; may be more mentholic/camphoraceous | stock and sensory HOLD | NOT AUTHORIZED |
| Nootkatone | Methyl Pamplemousse + Vetival across time | moderate recurrence gap; less exact/persistent grapefruit-vetiver link | NOT TESTED | NOT AUTHORIZED |
| Fractionated patchouli heart | Clearwood + restrained Patchouli EO | low-moderate rear-texture gap; potentially earthier/camphoraceous | NOT TESTED | NOT AUTHORIZED |
| Haitian vetiver | Indian Vetiver + Vetival | low-moderate register gap; deeper/earthier and less grapefruit-like | NOT TESTED | NOT AUTHORIZED |
| exact-basis ambroxide | nominal 33% w/v Ambrox Super | material function is present but exact w/w ppm/OAV is unresolved | basis/OAV HOLD | NOT AUTHORIZED |

No gap currently supports a purchase recommendation. Exact Pink Pepper is the only critical identity gap, but even that remains a contingent future comparison—not procurement authority.

## ODT, OAV, Composite-Natural, and Safety Holds

- Pink Pepper EO/Base repository thresholds are derived and the target material has no live supplier identity, physics, composite OAV, or safety authority. TARGET OAV is **HOLD**, never zero.
- Black Pepper EO, Peppermint Essential Oil, and Clary Sage EO have no exact-alias entry in the repository composite-natural registry. Their whole-mixture OAVs remain HOLD; any pipeline monomolecular result is a limited diagnostic.
- Habanolide has local MW/VP profile data and a `PEER_EST` 2.8 ppb air ODT; the material YAML has blank ODT fields. Pipeline resolution is computational and cannot establish comfort or intimacy.
- Rose Oxide and Damascone Beta may create literal rose/plum or high-activity takeover. Damascone remains at the 10 uL floor and needs material-specific safety review.
- Cedrat, Bergamot, BONTAUX Lavender, Indian Vetiver, Patchouli, and Labdanum exact aliases are present in the repository composite-natural registry. If the pipeline still displays a monomolecular or near-zero result for one of them, treat it as a data-path bypass/HOLD rather than proof of dormancy.
- Cyclamen is reduced from 50 to 20 uL because V1.2 modeled a Cat-4 edge. This is risk reduction, not safety clearance.
- Exact natural identities, lots, oxidation state, composite coverage, and formula-specific IFRA/allergen status remain unresolved until separately reviewed.

## Candidate-Survival Audit Before the V1.3 Run

| Candidate or change | Status entering final diagnostic | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| exact Pink Pepper TARGET | IDEAL-ONLY / DATA HOLD | unavailable; supplier-specific identity and composite model absent |
| CURRENT four-function reconstruction | KEEP FOR CONTROLLED TEST | distinct functions and explicit non-equivalence; sensory integration unknown |
| G glare-relief module | REBASE HYPOTHESIS | moves 230 uL of V1.2 lavender/citrus/fresh/muguet competition into declared negative space |
| S softened-pressure/release module | REBASE HYPOTHESIS | trades 110 uL of abstract/rigid rear pressure for middle movement/cushion without thinning Clearwood/Azarbre depth |
| Habanolide | REJECT DEFAULT / ADMIT ISOLATED HYPOTHESIS | one exact comfort role; must defeat Romandolide, EB, and no musk |
| Benzyl Benzoate +230 uL | STRUCTURAL EXCEPTION | declared negative-space compensator; not counted as audible complexity; detection invalidates causal claims |
| Hexyl Salicylate 300 uL | STRUCTURAL EXCEPTION | low-OAV cloth/cushion hypothesis below the first screen's safety edge; omission required |
| all five compression candidates | FINISHING CANDIDATES | retained only until 36-versus-31 and isolated add-backs |

## Citrus and Base Decision

V1.3 does **not** deepen the citruses. It halves the V1.2 Bergamot/Cedrat pair from 120 to 60 raw uL because V1.2 modeled Bergamot and Cedrat as major headspace competitors. The pair survives only as a floral-bitter edge and receives full/half/zero constant-total testing.

V1.3 also does **not** deepen the base by adding another material. It removes 110 raw uL from abstract or rigid rear pressure and reallocates exactly 110 uL to existing living-middle and cloth-release owners. Clearwood, Azarbre, vetiver, patchouli, Cashmeran, and trace Labdanum remain at V1.2 doses as the identity-bearing depth chain. The theory claim is not “less base”; it is **more perceived depth through pressure/release separation, not more amberwood mass**.

## Future Preparation Boundary

There is no authorized compounding. Before any future physical batch, re-read the full authority set, reconcile Ambrox and Peppermint stock bases, complete formula-specific safety review, record container IDs and oxidation state, and use the linked blinded protocol. Skin work remains separately gated.

### Future mixing order — basket by basket, high to low raw uL

1. **BASKET 1 — Always used:** Iso E Super (770), Hedione (600).
2. **BASKET 2 — Vetivers:** Vetiver EO India (230), Vetival (50).
3. **BASKET 3 — Woods:** Azarbre (300), Clearwood (270), Cashmeran (170), Patchouli EO (130), Timberol (100).
4. **BASKET 4 — Wood modifiers and ambers:** Ambrox Super (920), Benzyl Benzoate (330), Hexyl Salicylate (300), Labdanum Resinoid (100), Ambermax (70).
5. **BASKET 6 — Musks:** Habanolide (250).
6. **BASKET 7 — Muguet and lavender:** Lavender EO Bontaux (240), Linalyl Acetate (180), Ethyl Linalool (120), Helional (100), Clary Sage EO (60), Floralozone (40), Cyclamen Aldehyde (20).
7. **BASKET 8 — Jasmine, indole, and magnolia:** Dihydrojasmone (70).
8. **BASKET 10 — Rose:** Geraniol (30), Rose Oxide (20).
9. **BASKET 12 — Edible smells:** Coumarin (80).
10. **BASKET 13 — Edible spices:** Black Pepper EO (180).
11. **BASKET 15 — Fruits:** Bergamot FCF (40), Methyl Pamplemousse (40), Cedrat FCF (20), Damascone Beta (10).
12. **BASKET 16 — Aldehydes:** Dihydromyrcenol (60), Aldehyde C10 (30).
13. **BASKET 17 — Green smelling things:** Terpinyl Acetate (30), Peppermint EO (20), Scentenal (20).

Stir after each basket. Bring concentrate to exactly 6,000 uL. Add ethanol only under separately authorized physical compounding.

## Theory Decision

Silver Traverse V1.3 is admitted as a **34-row TARGET / 36-row CURRENT hedonic-rebase hypothesis**. It is the most deliberate hedonic version currently expressible in theory, not the most hedonic perfume established by evidence. Pink Pepper remains fixed as the protected hero. The revision subtracts likely glare and rigid pressure, creates more moving middle and declared negative space, and replaces the sole outward musk hypothesis with one inward comfort hypothesis. Every changed block is separable in the blinded plan.

**Final status:** THEORY ONLY / NOT TESTED / NO COMPOUNDING OR PROCUREMENT AUTHORIZED

## Pipeline Analysis

**Claim ceiling:** MODELED DIAGNOSTIC ONLY. Exact Pink Pepper cannot be modeled as current physical authority. Identity, equivalence, leadership, comfort, hedonism, liking, depth, diffusion, longevity, safety, stability, and release readiness remain **NOT TESTED** or **HOLD**.

